      "id": 1,
      "text": "Bush-Holley House, built around 1730, stands as the only National Historic Landmark in Greenwich, showcasing colonial architecture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cos_Cob%2C_Connecticut",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Cos Cob Railroad Station, built circa 1890, and the Mianus River Railroad Bridge, erected in 1904, are listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cos_Cob%2C_Connecticut",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Cos Cob Library serves as a community hub, offering an art gallery, concert and lecture series, and free Wi‑Fi for visitors.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cos_Cob%2C_Connecticut",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Cos Cob Harbor provides direct access to Long Island Sound, where tidal influences reach upstream into the Mianus River estuary.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
